{"id": "EUVD-2026-98692", "enisaUuid": "48c13fa6-7c30-3d84-a40c-be865273d2c3", "description": "yt-dlp-web-ui through 4.0.0 contains an argument injection vulnerability that allows unauthenticated remote attackers to inject yt-dlp options by supplying a dash-prefixed url parameter to the Service.Formats JSON-RPC method. Attackers can send values like --load-info-json via /rpc/http or /rpc/ws to make yt-dlp load attacker-chosen JSON files from the server filesystem, with contents reflected in responses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T14:00:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T14:00:17", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/vazzzy071-crypto/security-advisories/blob/main/advisories/2026-10-marcopiovanello-yt-dlp-web-ui-rpc-arg-injection.md", "https://github.com/marcopiovanello/yt-dlp-web-ui/blob/v4.0.0/server/formats/parser.go", "https://github.com/marcopiovanello/yt-dlp-web-ui", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/yt-dlp-web-ui-through-4.0.0-argument-injection-via-service-formats-json-rpc-method"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g8v9-4g6m-3vc9", "CVE-2026-109966"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.41, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ab56bc4-0007-3850-833f-3ae4f7f21fc3", "product": {"name": "yt-dlp-web-ui", "vendor": {"name": "marcopiovanello"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.0.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "20f8ac0e-28cb-353f-93f5-4007154b697a", "vendor": {"name": "marcopiovanello"}}], "isExploited": false}